.Dd $Mdocdate: September 11 2026 $
.Dt FUGUWEB 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fuguweb
.Nd build a documentation website for a Perl project
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm fuguweb
.Op Fl hq
.Op Fl Fl project Ar dir
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm fuguweb
.Cm init
.Op Ar dir
.Nm fuguweb
.Cm build
.Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
.Nm fuguweb
.Cm check
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
.Nm fuguweb
.Cm clean
.Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
.Nm fuguweb
.Cm rotate-key
.Fl Fl step Cm mint Ns | Ns Cm promote
.Fl Fl purpose Ar word
.Fl Fl secret Ar path
.Op Fl Fl signer Ar path
.Op Fl Fl org Ar word Oo Fl Fl dir Ar name Oc Op Fl Fl url Ar prefix
.Nm fuguweb
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
renders one static website from the documentation that a Perl project
already keeps:
.Xr mdoc 7
manuals, POD sidecars, and Markdown.
It runs
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
.Xr lowdown 1
and
.Xr pod2man 1 ,
and wraps each result in one shared page layout.
The output is plain HTML and one stylesheet.
There is no templating language and no JavaScript.
.Pp
A project is a directory that holds a
.Pa .fuguwebrc
file, the site description.
Without
.Fl Fl project ,
.Nm
searches up from the current directory for that file.
The directory that holds it is the project root.
Every relative path in the description, and a relative
.Fl Fl out ,
resolves against the project root.
.Pp
The build reads nothing from the network, writes nothing outside the
output directory, and gives the same bytes for the same checkout.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Print the usage message and exit.
.It Fl Fl project Ar dir
Use
.Ar dir
as the project root, and do not search for one.
.It Fl q , Fl Fl quiet
Do not print informational messages.
.El
.Pp
The commands are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Op Ar dir
Write a starter
.Pa .fuguwebrc
into
.Ar dir ,
which defaults to the current directory.
The starter names one page and one navigation entry, and it builds once
.Pa web/index.body.html
exists.
The command refuses a directory that already holds a description.
.It Cm build Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
Render the whole site into the output directory.
.Fl Fl out
overrides the
.Ic out_dir
setting.
.Pp
The command first checks that every renderer is installed, and names
the first one that is not.
It runs
.Xr mandoc 1
in lint mode over every mdoc source, and a warning fails the build.
It then writes the stylesheet, the assets, the key directory, each
page, and one page for each manual.
Last, it removes every file of the site that the description no longer
names, so a second build over one directory gives the same tree as the
first.
See
.Sx THE OUTPUT DIRECTORY .
.It Cm check Oo Fl v Oc Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
Check a built site.
The command prints one line for each problem and exits with status 5.
It prints nothing and exits with status 0 when the site is good.
.Pp
The checks are these:
every page and asset of the site exists and is not empty;
every page has a title and carries the whole navigation;
every local link, manual cross-reference, and fragment resolves;
no reference starts with a solidus, uses a
.Ql file\&:
URL, or reads as a URL scheme;
every page is reachable from the entry page, except a page marked
.Ic unlinked ;
and the output holds the site and nothing else, at any depth.
A description with a
.Ic keys
block adds the checks of
.Sx THE KEY DIRECTORY .
.Pp
.Fl v ,
.Fl Fl verbose
also prints every external link.
The command never fetches one.
.It Cm clean Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
Remove the output directory.
The command deletes a tree without asking, so it removes a built site
and refuses anything else.
See
.Sx THE OUTPUT DIRECTORY .
.Pp
With
.Fl Fl out
the command runs without a loadable description.
It then knows one flat directory of files, and it refuses a target that
holds no stylesheet, because every build writes one.
.It Xo Cm rotate-key
.Fl Fl step Cm mint Ns | Ns Cm promote
.Fl Fl purpose Ar word
.Fl Fl secret Ar path
.Op Fl Fl signer Ar path
.Op Fl Fl org Ar word Oo Fl Fl dir Ar name Oc Op Fl Fl url Ar prefix
.Xc
Mint the next
.Xr signify 1
key of a purpose, or promote the key that a mint made.
The command writes the key directory and the description.
See
.Sx KEY ROTATION .
.It Cm help Op Ar command
Print the usage of the tool, or of one command.
.El
.Sh THE SITE DESCRIPTION
The description is
.Pa .fuguwebrc
at the project root.
A setting is one
.Ar name No = Ar value
line.
A block opens with its type, a quoted name, and a brace, and closes
with a brace on a line of its own.
A
.Ql #
starts a comment, and no value can hold one.
.Pp
The settings are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "module_root" -offset indent
.It Ic site
The name of the site.
It ends the title of every page, and it is the text of the banner link.
This is the one required setting.
.It Ic lang
The
.Ql lang
attribute of every page.
The default is
.Ql en .
.It Ic out_dir
The output directory.
The default is
.Pa web/build .
.It Ic source_dir
The source directory.
The default is
.Pa web .
.It Ic entry
The front page, and the target of the banner link.
The default is
.Pa index.html .
.It Ic module_root
The prefix that a module name drops.
The default is
.Pa lib .
.It Ic mandoc_os
The operating system name in the footer of every rendered manual.
The default is
.Ql OpenBSD .
.It Ic man_url
The manual host for a cross-reference to a manual outside the site.
The default is
.Lk https://man.openbsd.org/ .
.It Ic stylesheet
The path of the base stylesheet.
By default the build searches for the sheet that ships with the tool.
.El
.Pp
A path setting must not step out of the project.
.Pp
The block types are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nav Qq Ar href
One navigation entry, on every page, in file order.
The block must set a
.Ic label .
.It Ic page Qq Ar file
One page of the site, named by its file in the output directory.
The name must be one path segment.
The block sets a
.Ic title ,
which defaults to the file name, and exactly one source:
.Bl -tag -width "markdown" -offset indent
.It Ic body
An HTML body fragment in the source directory.
.It Ic markdown
A Markdown file, relative to the project root.
.It Ic index No = Cm yes
The generated manual index.
.El
.Pp
.Ic unlinked No = Cm yes
marks a page that no other page links to, such as
.Pa 404.html ,
and the reachability check skips it.
.It Ic manuals Qq Ar heading
One group of
.Xr mdoc 7
manuals.
The block must set
.Ic dir ,
the directory of the sources, and
.Ic anchor ,
the fragment identifier of the group on the index page.
An optional
.Ic namespace
prefixes each manual name, so
.Pa man/fugu/Daemon.3p
with the namespace
.Ql Fugu:\&:
becomes
.Ql Fugu::Daemon(3p) .
.It Ic modules Qq Ar heading
One group of POD sidecars.
The block must set
.Ic dir
and
.Ic anchor ,
and
.Ic dir
must lie below
.Ic module_root .
.It Ic keys Qq Ar name
The published key directory.
See
.Sx THE KEY DIRECTORY .
.El
.Pp
The load fails when a block names no source or two sources, when two
blocks name one page, when a group directory does not exist, or when
the source directory holds a symlink.
Every message names the file and the block at fault.
.Sh THE PAGE LAYOUT
Every source becomes one HTML body fragment, and the build wraps each
fragment in one fixed layout: the head, a banner, the navigation, the
fragment, and a footer.
A project decides the site name, the language, the navigation, and the
footer prose.
.Pp
The title of a page is its own title, an em dash, and the site name.
The banner links the site name to the entry page.
The navigation lists each
.Ic nav
block, in file order.
.Pp
A
.Pa footer.body.html
in the source directory becomes the footer prose.
A project without one gets no footer element.
.Pp
The base stylesheet ships with the tool as
.Pa share/fuguweb/style.css .
The build copies it to
.Pa style.css
in the output directory, and every page links it under that name.
The
.Ic stylesheet
setting names another sheet.
A stylesheet that is not found fails the build.
.Sh MANUALS
A
.Ic manuals
group reads its directory for the plain files
.Pa *.1 ,
.Pa *.3p ,
.Pa *.5
and
.Pa *.8 .
It sorts them by section, in the order 1, 3p, 5, 8, and then by file
name.
The build renders each source with
.Xr mandoc 1
and names the page
.Ql <name>.<section>.html .
A cross-reference to a manual of the site becomes a local link.
Any other cross-reference links to the
.Ic man_url
host.
.Pp
A
.Ic modules
group finds every
.Pa .pod
file below its directory, and the sidecar that names the directory
itself:
.Pa lib/App/FuguWeb.pod
is the umbrella of
.Pa lib/App/FuguWeb/ .
The manual name is the path below
.Ic module_root
with
.Ql :\&:
between the segments, and the section is
.Ql 3p .
The build renders each sidecar with
.Xr pod2man 1
and then
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
so a module page carries the same layout as a hand-written manual.
The page date is the date of the last commit, from
.Xr git 1 .
A
.Ql L<>
reference renders as text, not as a link.
.Pp
The index page is the
.Ic page
block with
.Ic index No = Cm yes .
It opens with a paragraph that names the manual host.
A
.Pa manuals.body.html
in the source directory replaces that paragraph.
Each group then adds one heading with its
.Ic anchor ,
and one list of its manuals.
Each entry links the page and shows the one-line description, from the
first
.Ic \&Nd
macro of an mdoc source or the
.Sy NAME
section of a sidecar.
A group with no manual adds nothing.
.Sh THE SOURCE DIRECTORY
The source directory holds the body fragments, the footer, and the
assets.
Every plain file directly in it that the build does not render is an
asset, and the build copies it as it stands.
A
.Pa *.body.html
fragment, a
.Pa *.md
file, and a dot file are not assets.
.Pa robots.txt
and
.Pa CNAME
therefore need no entry in the description, and notes for the
maintainers are not published.
.Pp
The build rejects a symlink in the source directory.
A copy would publish the bytes of the target, from anywhere on the
machine.
.Sh THE OUTPUT DIRECTORY
The output is one flat directory of files.
The key directory and the well-known tree are the only parts below the
top level.
.Pp
The build writes plain files only.
It refuses a symlink on any path that it writes, before it writes one
file.
It owns a plain file at the top level, a file that the site names, and
a file that has a shape of the key directory.
It keeps every other entry, reports it, and never removes it.
.Cm clean
removes what the build owns, and a directory of the site or of the key
tree.
It refuses every other entry, and names it, so it never removes a file
that the build keeps.
.Pp
Both
.Cm build
and
.Cm clean
refuse a target that no build may own: the root of the filesystem, the
home directory, the project root, and any directory that holds the
project.
They refuse the source directory and every directory below it.
The output directory of the description is the one exception, because
the default output directory sits inside the default source directory.
.Pp
The build stages every manual source in
.Pa .man
inside the output directory, so that
.Xr mandoc 1
resolves a cross-reference against the manuals of the site.
The build removes the staging directory when it ends.
It refuses a staging directory of another shape, and so does
.Cm clean .
.Sh THE KEY DIRECTORY
An organization publishes its public keys under one prefix, so a
consumer can fetch a key and verify a release with it.
A
.Ic keys
block describes that directory, and the build publishes it.
A description holds at most one such block.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
keys "keys" {
	org     = fugubsd
	contact = mailto:security@fugubsd.org
	expires = 2027-09-07T00:00:00Z
	url     = https://www.fugubsd.org/keys
}

key "fugubsd-1-release" {
	status = current
	since  = 2026-09-07
}
.Ed
.Pp
The block name is the directory, one path segment below the source
directory.
The settings are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "contact" -offset indent
.It Ic org
The organization word, the first field of every key name.
This setting is required.
.It Ic contact
The
.Ql Contact
field of
.Pa security.txt .
.It Ic expires
The
.Ql Expires
field of
.Pa security.txt ,
an RFC 3339 timestamp.
.Ic contact
and
.Ic expires
stand or fall together.
.It Ic url
The published prefix of the directory, an absolute URL.
.El
.Pp
Each
.Ic key
block names the stem of one key file in the directory.
The file extension gives the type:
.Pa .pub
is a
.Xr signify 1
key, and
.Pa .asc
is an armored OpenPGP key.
The block sets a
.Ic status
of
.Cm current ,
.Cm next
or
.Cm retired ,
and optional
.Ic since
and
.Ic until
dates.
An OpenPGP key can set an
.Ic email
and a
.Ic fingerprint
of 40 hexadecimal characters.
.Pp
The directory must hold a
.Pa SHA256
manifest and its
.Pa SHA256.sig
signature.
The build copies each key file and the manifest pair byte for byte.
It signs nothing and verifies nothing.
For the example above it generates these files:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width ".well-known/openpgpkey/hu/<hash>" -offset indent -compact
.It Pa keys/KEYS
Every OpenPGP key, when the set holds one.
.It Pa keys/index.html
The human page, with the serial, purpose, type, status, fingerprint,
and dates of each key.
.It Pa .well-known/openpgpkey/hu/<hash>
The Web Key Directory file of each email address.
.It Pa .well-known/openpgpkey/policy
The Web Key Directory policy file.
.It Pa .well-known/security.txt
The RFC 9116 file, when the block sets a
.Ic contact .
.El
.Pp
.Cm check
reads the source key directory, so the answer does not depend on a
build.
It checks that every key file has a block and every block has a file,
that every name matches the key name pattern, that every purpose holds
exactly one current key, that the manifest names every key file with
the digest that it has and nothing else, that every declared
fingerprint equals the computed one, and that the signature has the
shape of a
.Xr signify 1
signature.
.Sh KEY ROTATION
A consumer verifies a release against the copy of the public key that
it holds.
A release that a new key signs therefore fails in each consumer that
holds the old copy.
One rotation runs in two steps.
.Pp
.Fl Fl step Cm mint
generates the next key of the purpose with
.Xr signify 1 ,
writes its public half into the key directory, and writes its private
half to
.Fl Fl secret
with no group and no other permissions.
The new key takes the status
.Cm next ,
and the current key of the purpose signs the manifest.
.Fl Fl signer
names the private half of that current key.
.Fl Fl secret
must not name a file that exists, and must not name the signer.
A mint refuses a purpose that already holds a
.Cm next
key.
.Pp
The first mint of a purpose finds no current key.
The new key is current at once, signs its own manifest, and takes no
.Fl Fl signer .
A site with no
.Ic keys
block takes one from the command line:
.Fl Fl org
names the organization word,
.Fl Fl dir
names the directory, which defaults to
.Pa keys ,
and
.Fl Fl url
names the published prefix.
.Pp
.Fl Fl step Cm promote
makes the
.Cm next
key of the purpose current, and retires the key that was current with
an
.Ic until
date.
.Fl Fl secret
names the private half of the key that becomes current, and that key
signs the manifest.
A retired key keeps its file and its URL, so a release that it signed
still verifies.
.Pp
Every key of one directory holds one purpose, because one key signs the
whole manifest.
Each step verifies the new signature against the published public key
of the signer before one byte reaches the key directory, and a step
that fails puts every file back.
On success the command prints one
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
line for each fact: the file name, the stem, the serial, the status,
and the retired name of a promote.
.Pp
The command reaches no network and holds no token.
The caller stores the private key and commits the public one.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "share/fuguweb/style.css" -compact
.It Pa .fuguwebrc
The site description, at the project root.
.It Pa share/fuguweb/style.css
The base stylesheet, which ships with the tool.
.It Pa web/footer.body.html
The footer prose, in the default source directory.
.It Pa web/manuals.body.html
The opening of the manual index, in the default source directory.
.It Pa web/build/.man
The staging directory of the build, in the default output directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with one of the following values:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -offset indent -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
General error.
.It 2
Invalid arguments.
.It 3
Configuration error, or no
.Pa .fuguwebrc
found.
.It 4
The build failed: a renderer failed, or a manual source is malformed.
.It 5
The check found a problem.
.It 6
A renderer, or
.Xr signify 1 ,
is not installed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start a site, build it, and check it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fuguweb init
$ fuguweb build
$ fuguweb check
.Ed
.Pp
Build into another directory, from anywhere in the project:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fuguweb build --out /tmp/site
$ fuguweb check --out /tmp/site
.Ed
.Pp
Publish the first release key of an organization:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fuguweb rotate-key --step mint --purpose release \e
	--secret ~/keys/release-1.sec --org fugubsd \e
	--url https://www.fugubsd.org/keys
.Ed
.Pp
Rotate the release key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fuguweb rotate-key --step mint --purpose release \e
	--secret ~/keys/release-2.sec --signer ~/keys/release-1.sec
$ fuguweb rotate-key --step promote --purpose release \e
	--secret ~/keys/release-2.sec
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lowdown 1 ,
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
.Xr pod2man 1 ,
.Xr signify 1 ,
.Xr mdoc 7
.Pp
The module documentation is in the
.Pa .pod
sidecars beside
.Pa lib/App/FuguWeb/ .
